# Streams 1 & 2 Audit Dossier — PM/Registry and LSP/Tree-Sitter

// Logline: Negative-Trust audit dossier of Stream 1 (Sovereign Package Manager) and Stream 2 (Sovereign LSP and Tree-Sitter); every claim is E2E proven and double-run certified per RULES §1.9 and WORKFLOW §3.

// Setup: 2026-08-23. Active Falsification applied: every proof below was run twice in `env -i PATH=/usr/bin:/bin` clean shells and the bytes compared. AST Honesty: this dossier names the live workarounds for oodac C-emit bugs (`let r: Result<String,String> = sys_exec(...)` triggers on 3+ uses in one TU; `List<String>` cross-file parameters drop; `match r { Ok(s) => s, Err(m) => m }` on `sys_exec` Result is mis-emitted). Sources cross-referenced against the bytes: ooda/cli/*.oo, ooda/lsp/*.oo, ooda/runtime/chs_rt_fs.c, tree-sitter/grammar.js, tree-sitter/parse_probe.js, registry/*, openOODA/SHIPPED.oot, openOODA/RULES.oot. Per RULES 1.9 (Negative Trust) and the 5 Invariant Axioms, board text is not proof; this dossier cites the on-disk bytes and the double-run outputs.

