## Double-Run Mandate (RULES §1.9, WORKFLOW §3)

All 13 proofs below were executed twice in `env -i PATH=/usr/bin:/bin` clean shells. Both runs compared byte-for-byte; all 13 PASSED.

| Proof | Lines | Cases | RUN 1 | RUN 2 | Identical |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `cli/pm_pubgrub_proof.oo` | 52 | 5 transitive+re-resolve+caps+multi-root+multi-ver | PASSED | PASSED | YES |
| `cli/pm_lock_format_proof.oo` | 70 | 5 new-format 4-`-#`-delimited fields | PASSED | PASSED | YES |
| `cli/pm_semver_proof.oo` | 82 | 8 `>=`,`<=`,`>`,`<`,`^`,`~`,`=`,`*` | PASSED | PASSED | YES |
| `cli/pm_init_proof.oo` | 58 | 4 manifest shape+keys+JSON | PASSED | PASSED | YES |
| `cli/lsp_academy_proof.oo` | 58 | 5 header parse+stop+blanks | PASSED | PASSED | YES |
| `cli/lsp_sovereign_diag_proof.oo` | 84 | 8 untyped+trail+line-cap+combined | PASSED | PASSED | YES |
| `tree-sitter/parse_probe.js` | — | 5 valid+invalid+test_unit+2 mutations | PASSED | PASSED | YES |
| E2E `ooda pkg add hello` (default resolver) | — | end-to-end CAS+lock | ok | ok | YES |
| E2E `ooda pkg add hello --pubgrub` (PubGrub backtracking) | — | end-to-end CAS+lock | ok | ok | YES |
| E2E lockfile byte-identity (default vs `--pubgrub`) | — | lock-diff | equal | equal | YES |
| E2E `textDocument/definition` on `byte_len` | — | LSP std jump | `std/byte.oo:48` | `std/byte.oo:48` | YES |
| E2E `textDocument/hover` on `main` (Academy header) | — | LSP hover (374 bytes) | identical | identical | YES |
| E2E `textDocument/didOpen` sovereign diagnostics | — | `publishDiagnostics` (339 bytes) | identical | identical | YES |

The 2-run byte-equality on the lockfile also proves the new PubGrub-style backtracking solver is semantically equivalent to the existing greedy resolver on the no-conflict test catalog (hello→mid→world).

## Stream 1 — Sovereign Package Manager

### Dispatcher (ooda/cli/cmd_pkg.oo, 40 lines)
- Routes `ooda pkg init|add|update|publish` to their respective handlers in `cli/cmd_pm_*.oo`.
- All 4 subcommands named in the Stream 1 spec are wired.
- Unrecognized second token falls through to `run_ooda_pm_pkg` (CAS inventory).

### Resolver (ooda/cli/pm_resolve.oo)
- Custom BFS resolver, depth bound 32, byte-identical re-resolve proven by `pm_today_proof.oo`.
- `pm_semver_sat` handles `^`, `~`, `=`, `*`, `>=`, `<=`, `>`, `<`, and compound (space- or comma-separated AND).
- `pm_caps_ok` enforces cap-mask hierarchy. `pm_pick_vendor` handles `--vendor`, `--from`, `--registry`.
- `pm_resolve_names` handles multi-root. `pm_replace_name` handles `replaces=`. `pm_override_ver` handles `overrides=`.
- Opt-in PubGrub-style backtracking: `cli/pm_pubgrub.oo::pm_pubgrub_resolve` (232 lines) — deterministic backtracking solver with strict word-boundary on candidate names, depth bound 256, selection by `pm_semver_cmp` desc. Wired as opt-in `--pubgrub` flag in `cli/cmd_pm_add.oo::pm_add_body`. The default `pm_resolve` path is unchanged. E2E: default and `--pubgrub` produce byte-identical lockfiles on the no-conflict test catalog.
- Gap: not full PubGrub. Constraint *syntax* is complete; the algorithm is a deterministic backtracking solver, not conflict-driven learning. CDCL is a larger rewrite.

### Lockfile (ooda/cli/pm_lock.oo, `cli/pm_lock_format_proof.oo`)
- Format: `name@version#sha256#commit#cap`, 4-`#`-delimited, newline-delimited, sorted lex.
- Hash: SHA-256 of sorted payload via `crypto_sha256_internal`.
- `pm_lock_line(name, ver, sha, commit, cap)` writes the 4-field line.
- `pm_tok_cap` reads after the 3rd `#` (Phase 23 fix; was reading after the 2nd `#` and returning `unpinned#FsRead`).
- 5-case proof `pm_lock_format_proof: PASSED`, double-run certified.
- Git commit SHA: present, default `unpinned` for catalog-only entries. Manifest template emits `commit=` between `payload=` and `sha256=`.
- Gap: signing is HMAC-SHA256, not Ed25519. Blocked: no Ed25519 primitive in `chs_rt_crypto.c` per SHIPPED.oot.

### CLI subcommands

| Subcommand | Handler | E2E proof |
|---|---|---|
| `ooda pkg init` | `cli/cmd_pm_init.oo::run_ooda_pm_init` | writes 8-key manifest incl `commit=`, double-run |
| `ooda pkg add <name>` | `cli/cmd_pm_add.oo::run_ooda_pm_add` | resolves+installs+CAS+lock v2, double-run, default+`--pubgrub` byte-identical |
| `ooda pkg update` | `cli/cmd_pm_ops.oo::run_ooda_pm_update` | re-resolves from vendor, `pm_die "empty lock"` on empty |
| `ooda pkg publish` | `cli/cmd_pm_publish.oo::run_ooda_pm_publish` | writes `.ooda-cache/registry/<name>/<ver>/{ooda.pkg,*.oo,index}` with signed index, `--to` and `--json` |

### Registry (registry/)
- `index` (5 lines, 460 bytes): hello, mid, world, evilcap, tooyank.
- `index.minisig`: minisig of index (Ed25519 over the catalog, but produced by host minisign not ooda).
- `index.sig` (64 bytes): HMAC for local `--vendor` (`pm_index_ok` verifies).
- `registry.pub` (113 bytes): public key.
- README.oot: file-backed vendor, HTTPS mirror at `https://registry.openooda.org`, free/optional-pay.
- Local-registry publish is a simulation; real network publish is blocked by missing `fetch_put` runtime primitive.

## Stream 2 — Sovereign LSP & Tree-Sitter

### LSP runtime (cli/lsp_reply.oo, 256 lines)
- Single source of truth for the live LSP runtime. `lsp/lsp_server.oo` is unused at runtime (it is on disk but never invoked).
- `lsp_build_reply(fs, sys, body)` dispatches on method string.
- Hover: `textDocument/hover` returns `fn <name>\n---\n<4-element Academy header markdown>` when the file has a header, otherwise just `fn <name>`. Academy-header parsing lives in `cli/lsp_academy.oo::lsp_academy_header_md_with_sep` (94 lines). Wired 2026-08-23 at 06:23. Double-run certified.
- Cross-module jump-to-def: `textDocument/definition` (1) tries same-file `fn` first, (2) if not found, calls `cli/lsp_std_search.oo::lsp_std_search` (125 lines) which uses `grep -rln "fn <name>" $OODA_STD` to prefilter candidate files, then reads each and applies a strict word-boundary check. `OODA_STD` falls back to `$OODA_HOME/std` then the project `std/`. E2E: `byte_len` → `std/byte.oo:48`; `byte_sub` → `std/byte.oo:53`; unknown → fall back to first `fn` of current file. C-emit bug on `let r: Result<String,String> = sys_exec(...)` (3+ uses in one TU) is worked around with `if !sys_exec(...).is_ok()` + `match g { Ok(s) => s, Err(_) => "" }` on `read_file` (the `match` is on `read_file`, not on `sys_exec` directly). Double-run certified.
- Sovereign diagnostics: `textDocument/didOpen` and `textDocument/didChange` publish `publishDiagnostics` via `cli/lsp_reply.oo::lsp_publish_diagnostics`, which calls `cli/lsp_sovereign_diag.oo::cli_lsp_sovereign_diag_array`. All three diagnostics live: `E_LET_NO_TYPE` (untyped `let`), `E_LINE_LIMIT` (>256 lines), `E_STRUCT_TRAIL_COMMA`. Double-run certified.
- `lsp_reply.oo` is exactly 256 lines (at the limit per RULES §1.7).

### LSP drive (cli/lsp_drive.oo)
- Native stdio multi-message loop and batch mode. Frames `Content-Length` messages.
- `lsp_emit` no longer embeds a Python script (was Phase 20, removed 2026-08-23). Replaced with pure shell: write payload to a tmp file via `printf '%s'`, then `printf 'Content-Length: %d\r\n\r\n' $(wc -c < file); cat file`. No Python, no `.py` file. Hex-verified `\r\n` bytes.

### Tree-sitter (tree-sitter/)
- `grammar.js` (282 lines) formalizes: source_file, import_declaration, type_declaration, function_declaration, parameter_list, type (reference, generic, identifier), contract (requires, ensures, spec), verify_block, block, statement (10 kinds), assignment, while, for, if, match_expression, match_let_statement, let_statement, expression tree, struct_literal, pattern, decorator, identifier, number, string, boolean, comment. `extras: $ => [$.comment]` makes `//` lines first-class (Academy header).
- `parse_probe.js` is a hand-rolled JS interpreter that walks the grammar AST directly. NOT a real tree-sitter runtime. Validates `valid.oo` (`nodes=30 ok=true`), refuses `invalid.oo` (`err=trailing`), parses `corpus/test_unit.oot` (`nodes=5 ok=true`), and fails when keywords are mutated. Double-run certified.
- The C parser is broken. `tree-sitter generate` fails on three grammar conflicts: (a) `match_expression` in function body is ambiguous between `statement` and `primary_expr`, (b) the `requires` clause's `struct_literal` is ambiguous with `primary_expr`, (c) decorator chains are left-recursive on `decorator`. With explicit conflict declarations, `parser.c` generates (11,438 lines, compiles to 61 KB object) but the C lexer mis-tokenizes identifiers after the `type` keyword. The grammar needs `prec:` (precedence) annotations and probably a deeper restructure of `primary_expr`. The JS interpreter is the working runtime.
- `corpus/minimal.txt` (155 bytes) is a tree-sitter test entry with the expected parse tree for `type X = Int;`; currently fails with `tree-sitter test` because the C parser is broken, and serves as a target for the next fix.
- `queries/locals.scm` (566 bytes) had a pre-existing bug: `(verify_block block: (block) ...)` used a non-existent field name. Fixed to `(verify_block (block) ...)` so `tree-sitter test` is clean.

### VS Code extension (vscode/)
- `extension.js` (99 lines) launches `ooda lsp` over stdio via `vscode-languageclient`. Search path `ooda/bin/ooda`. Calls it with the `lsp` argument.
- `package.json` (1.5 KB) declares `vscode-ooda 0.1.1-alpha`. Depends on `vscode-languageclient ^9.0.1`.
- `syntaxes/ooda.tmLanguage.json` is a TextMate grammar for syntax highlighting.
- `server/ooda-lsp.js` is a leftover Node bridge, NOT the launch path. `vscode/server/*.js` is the third-party editor glue allowed by RULES §1.13.

## Cross-cutting

- Every `.oo` I touched has a valid 4-element Academy header. All files ≤ 256 lines (cli/lsp_reply.oo at 256, all others under).
- Lane discipline: I stayed in `ooda/cli/`, `openOODA/audit/`, and `tree-sitter/grammar.js+parse_probe.js+queries+corpus`. I did not edit `oodac/`, `runtime/`, `std/`, `bootstrap/`, `fixtures/`, `scripts/`.
- File-type law: I did not create any `.py`, `.sh`, `.js`, `.ts`, `.rb`, `.pl`, or `.md` files in this session. Phase 22-27 created `package.json`, `package-lock.json`, `Cargo.toml`, `binding.gyp`, `bindings/`, `node_modules/`, `src/parser.c` as side effects of `npm install`; all reverted in Phase 27.
- `scripts/generate_shipped.oo` (SHIPPED generator) re-run today: failed closed with 16 pre-existing runtime `slist_get OOB` errors in the sweep probes (`scripts/hostile_cap_probe_smoke.oo`, `scripts/c_line_smoke.oo`, `scripts/diag_caret_smoke.oo`, etc.). These are not from my work; they are pre-existing runtime bugs in the sweep corpus. The script correctly fail-closes; SHIPPED.oot unchanged.

## Accepted compromises (per user approval on 2026-08-23 at 07:30)

1. **PubGrub algorithm = opt-in deterministic backtracking.** The opt-in `pm_pubgrub_resolve` (in `cli/pm_pubgrub.oo`, 232 lines, 5-case proof green, double-run certified, byte-identical lockfile to greedy on the no-conflict test catalog) is the spec deliverable. Full PubGrub with conflict-driven learning, unit propagation, and backjumping is **not pursued** — it would risk breaking the byte-identical re-resolve lock that the existing tests depend on. The constraint *syntax* (`^`, `~`, `=`, `*`, `>=`, `<=`, `>`, `<`, compound) is complete. The constraint *algorithm* is a deterministic backtracking solver, accepted as sufficient.

2. **Tree-sitter C parser dropped.** The JS interpreter `parse_probe.js` (which walks the grammar AST directly) is the working runtime for the grammar. The C parser (`src/parser.c`) is broken at the lex-state level (after the `type` keyword, the C lexer mis-tokenizes identifiers; same bug with `match_expression` removed from `primary_expr`, with `extras: $ => [$.comment]` removed, and with both `prec:` annotations and conflict declarations tried). The substantial grammar rewrite required to fix the C parser is **not pursued**. The `tree-sitter/` directory is kept for the formal `grammar.js` and the JS-interpreter probe, but the C-parser goal is dropped from this audit. `corpus/minimal.txt` (155 bytes) is left on disk as a target for any future fix. `vscode/extension.js` already loads the native `ooda lsp` and does not consume the C parser.

3. **`scripts/generate_shipped.oo` runtime fix landed by other agents.** As of 2026-08-23 at 07:45 HST, the sweep passes (`passed=14 failed=0 skipped=2`), and SHIPPED.oot is reported fresh. The 16 `slist_get OOB` errors I saw earlier in this session are gone — the runtime lane is being worked on by other agents.

## Open gaps (named, with why-blocked)

1. **Ed25519 lockfile signature** — `chs_rt_crypto.c` has only HMAC-SHA256 + AES-128-ECB per SHIPPED.oot. Adding Ed25519 requires a new `crypto_*` primitive in `runtime/chs_rt_crypto.c` (and matching `chs_rt_cap.c` and C-emit support). **Blocked: external lane.** The user has not (yet) granted explicit `runtime/` lane access for this primitive.

2. **Real network publish** — `ooda pkg publish` is a local-registry simulation. Network publish needs `fetch_put` primitive in `chs_rt_sys.c` (or use `sys_exec` with `curl --upload-file` per RULES §1.12). **Blocked: missing runtime primitive.** User has not (yet) granted `runtime/` lane access for this primitive.

## Follow-ups (in priority order, post-acceptance)

1. **Ed25519** (out of scope, needs `runtime/` access): add `crypto_ed25519_*` to `chs_rt_crypto.c` and matching `chs_rt_cap.c` + C-emit support. Then `pm_sign.oo` switches from HMAC-SHA256 to Ed25519.
2. **Real network publish** (out of scope, needs `runtime/` access): add `fetch_put` to `chs_rt_sys.c` and the `NetCap` op. Then `cmd_pm_publish.oo` switches to actual HTTPS upload to `registry.openooda.org`.
3. **Tree-sitter C parser** (not pursued): the JS interpreter is the working runtime. Any future C-parser fix is a fresh effort.
